{title: Come, Thou Long-Expected Jesus}
{artist: Charles Wesley}
{genre: Christmas}
{style: Hymn}
{flow: Opening}
{key: F}
{tempo: 84}
{time: 4/4}
{score: come-thou-long-expected-jesus.abc}

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[F]Come, Thou long-ex[Dm]pected Jesus
[Bb]Born to set Thy [F]people free
[F]From our fears and [Dm]sins release us
[Bb]Let us find our [C]rest in [F]Thee
[F]Israel's strength and [Dm]consolation
[Bb]Hope of all the [F]earth Thou art
[F]Dear desire of [Dm]every nation
[Bb]Joy of every [C]longing [F]heart
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[F]Born Thy people [Dm]to deliver
[Bb]Born a child and [F]yet a King
[F]Born to reign in [Dm]us forever
[Bb]Now Thy gracious [C]kingdom [F]bring
[F]By Thine own e[Dm]ternal Spirit
[Bb]Rule in all our [F]hearts alone
[F]By Thine all-suf[Dm]ficient merit
[Bb]Raise us to Thy [C]glorious [F]throne
{end_of_verse}
